      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author decomposes geometric satisfaction instances by partition trees, recursively combines special feasible solutions and solves bounded-height leaf instances by dynamic programming. The full feasibility, approximation and running-time recurrences are retained, including the stated online adaptation. This positive cost-time algorithm theorem is distinct from the existing negative strong-Wilber gap construction; the published retraction of conference complexity consequences is preserved and not asserted anew.",
